+//!     R(T)  = [e(T) - e0] - (c/chat) a (E0 - B(T)) / (1 + a)
+//! MONOTONICALLY INCREASING in T (e(T) rises; B rises so -(E0-B) rises), so a bracketed method
+//! on it is guaranteed to converge. Used ONLY as the non-convergence fallback below.
